---
name: clearqueue-reject-on-clear
description: p-limit clearQueue drops pending promises unresolved by default; rejectOnClear rejects them with an AbortError
type: project
---
p-limit's `clearQueue()` behavior depends on the `rejectOnClear` option, which defaults to `false` (`let rejectOnClear = false;` plus destructuring from an options object, and a `TypeError` unless it is a boolean) and never cancels already-running promises:

```js
if (!rejectOnClear) {
	queue.clear();
	return;
}

const abortError = AbortSignal.abort().reason;

while (queue.size > 0) {
	queue.dequeue().reject(abortError);
}
```

- With the default `rejectOnClear: false`, `queue.clear()` discards pending items without settling them, so a caller that still awaits those promises never sees them resolve or reject after `clearQueue()`.
